{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic","id":1179633,"title":"How does quiescence work in a society that believes in magic?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-26T15:17:53-08:00","id":1179633,"title":"How does quiescence work in a society that believes in magic?","content":"At first I thought that quiescence affected sleepers exclusively exposed to supernal magic, however the 2E book and some other source material such as Magical Traditions suggest that even sleeper or sleepwalker magic contains motes of the supernal, or that it is a fallen version of the supernal in a sense. According to the sourcebook, some mediums and fallen magic practitioners would be sleepwalkers. The other supernaturals would also be sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to this question, how would quiescence work in a society where everyone believes in magic, even sleepwalker magic? For example, almost any society prior to the Renaissance, or even many more traditional societies today. Also I could see that in remote villages that still rely on traditional healers, if someone were to awaken, they potentially could practice in the open if they community accepts it. Maybe many spiritual traditions and religions were awakened trying to explain their enlightenment to their communities.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <b>I should emphasize that these traditional practitioners who aren't awakened aren't just humans with wishful thinking, but could be low magic practitioners as in the Second Sight book.</b><br /> <br /> To be honest, the attitude of quiescence toward magic seems mostly a way that modern people sometimes respond to the supernatural, of course mostly those who are invested in a worldview that does not allow for magic, and not the person who chases the latest New Age fad. An alternate way it could manifest especially in people who do believe in the supernatural, would be more akin to lunacy or disquiet, with great fear and belief the mage is corrupted by an evil spirit.<br /> <br /> Yet it gets murky with the division between sleeper and sleepwalker. I could argue that long ago, sleepwalkers were the norm if belief in magic was the norm, or would it be?<br /> <br /> I am playing a mage who is into archeology and anthropology, she works at a natural history museum and routinely handles &quot;sleeper magic&quot; objects, so I thought that this question might be an interesting obsession for her.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I already know that belief isn't what divides a sleeper and a sleepwalker, but rather I am talking about <b>exposure</b> to the supernatural or even tiny fragments of the supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","user":"GreenKitty","date":". 01-26-2018, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","name":"GreenKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23750_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T15:20:57-08:00","id":1179636,"title":"","content":"The Sleeper/Sleepwalker divide is not the same as the believer/nonbeliever divide: there are many, many Sleepers who believe in magic. Sleepwalker status has nothing to do with belief, beyond the fact that it's hard to maintain disbelief when supporting evidence is all around you (which is why disbelieving Sleepwalkers are rare).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-26-2018, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T15:23:33-08:00","id":1179638,"title":"","content":"Sleepwalker magic isn\u2019t Supernal unless you\u2019re specifically referring to the Blessings of Proximi.<br /> <br /> For an in depth answer to your question though you could read To The Strongest from Dark Eras which has Neolithic groups living with Mages who are publicly known. The short answer though is that the Mage is taken for granted as being able to work magic because their magic has results, but they have to practice their art in private.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T15:24:49-08:00","id":1179639,"title":"","content":"Such a culture may have more than their normal population of Sleepwalkers, but other than that, nothing special.<br /> <br /> The shard of the Abyss isn't excised by simply believing in Magic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T15:25:45-08:00","id":1179640,"title":"","content":"Belief has nothing to do with it. Even in the Neolithic era, where the supernatural outright walked together with mortals and mages were venerated as the Wise men and women of the village, mages still had to work their more potent miracles away from Sleepers. And the demarcation of Sleeper and Sleepwalker stems from neither perspective nor belief, but whether one has (non-Supernal) been touched by the supernatural themselves, the minimim bar for the supernatural touch being \u201cMy mind doesn\u2019t break from experiencing the Supernal/Abyssal.\u201d<br /> <br /> Of course, this doesn\u2019t stop in-universe mages from believing otherwise. Especially if they\u2019re Free Council (who believe Culture is Magical) or Silver Ladder (who believe Magic is Humanity\u2019s Birthright).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T15:51:10-08:00","id":1179646,"title":"","content":"Yes, I do understand that belief isn't the division between sleeper and sleepwalker.<br /> <br /> I should have emphasized something, and that is if you are talking about communities with <b>bona fide magic practitioners</b>-witchdoctors, mediums, thaumaturges, miracle-workers, etc. that is, ones with &quot;low magic&quot; already going around, and one that works according to more &quot;low magic&quot; rules such as those found in Second Sight.<br /> <br /> Also, in Mirrors: Infinite Macabre, it suggests that a wide belief in magic and the weird can reduce paradox. <br /> <br /> And so how does a sleeper become a sleepwalker?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","user":"GreenKitty","date":". 01-26-2018, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","name":"GreenKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23750_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:03:53-08:00","id":1179648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreenKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179646#post1179646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I do understand that belief isn't the division between sleeper and sleepwalker.<br /> <br /> I should have emphasized something, and that is if you are talking about communities with <b>bona fide magic practitioners</b>-witchdoctors, mediums, thaumaturges, miracle-workers, etc. that is, ones with &quot;low magic&quot; already going around, and one that works according to more &quot;low magic&quot; rules such as those found in Second Sight.<br /> <br /> Also, in Mirrors: Infinite Macabre, it suggests that a wide belief in magic and the weird can reduce paradox. <br /> <br /> And so how does a sleeper become a sleepwalker?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the society is composed entirely of Sleepwalkers and Awakened, then no Quiescence. No Dissonance. An ambitious mage\u2019s wet dream. <br /> <br /> EDIT: \u201cEntirely\u201d is the important word here. Just having a lot of non-Supernal sorcerers running around in a community will do nothing to alleviate the Sleeping Curse for Sleepers in the community, nor for outsider Sleepers visiting it. No Reality Zones here. <br /> <br /> The mention in Mirrors was made when Dissonance was still called Disbelief, so I highly doubt it being canon in 2E, much like how the \u201cArcadia Question\u201d is now firmly answered with \u201cNo.\u201d I\u2019d consider it a relic of 1E... but I admit, the story hook potential in it remains too tantalizing to ignore.<br /> <br /> Out-of-game, just buy the Sleepwalker or Fitful Slumber Merit, a Supernatural Merit, or outright get a supernatural template like Wolf-Blooded or Vampire. In-universe, it involves internalizing supernatural power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 01-26-2018, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:31:12-08:00","id":1179654,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> , I guess that sort of is were some of my questions stem from is that lore differences exist in 1e and 2e, yet most of the material out there was done when it was 1e and some corebook lines are still in 1e. And yet, much of what addresses these ideas are in those supplement books. For example, the supplement book Magical Traditions shows a dialogue between a supposed sleepwalker and a mystagogue, wherein the mystagogue dismisses the sleepwalker's story and brushes it off, but the sleepwalker insists the power lies in the story.<br /> <br /> Another question though, and I guess this is something that depends on the ST a lot-is just how common low magic users were compared to wannabe magic practitioners out there back in the old days or in societies that still steep with belief in magic. Some people get the impression that even long ago, magic was something esoteric, especially something like the Lesser Key of Solomon. However I know that &quot;traditional magic&quot; was an everyday thing, such as Appalachian &quot;Granny Magic&quot; and Hoodoo, and still is in many parts of the world. I would assume that given the World of Darkness and how it is, that many of these practitioners would produce results and would tap into the supernatural due to the existence of spirits, ghosts, ESP, and well. that it exists.<br /> <br /> Or would they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","user":"GreenKitty","date":". 01-26-2018, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","name":"GreenKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23750_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:41:59-08:00","id":1179659,"title":"","content":"If a person had some form of hoodoo magic and used it to cure the sick they of course would not cause Dissonance, right? Right. Now let's even assume that this is a place where such 'hoodoo magic' was common and widely accepted. If an Awakened mage dressed up in all of the hoodoo trappings, went through all the hoodoo motions, healed the exact same sort of wound for the exact same person in the exact same circumstances but used Supernal magic instead, it would *still* trigger Dissonance in the person/people watching.<br /> <br /> As for how common and believed magic and stuff was way back when and in some places even in modern day. Magic was essentially as accepted as true as science is today. It was a fact of life. How 'true' these instances of magic were/are is indeed going to be up to ST fiat though. It depends on the needs of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 01-26-2018, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:43:29-08:00","id":1179660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179659#post1179659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a person had some form of hoodoo magic and used it to cure the sick they, of course, would not cause Dissonance. Let's even assume that this is a place where such 'hoodoo magic' was common and widely accepted. If an Awakened mage dressed up in all of the hoodoo trappings, went through all the hoodoo motions, healed the exact same sort of wound for the exact same person in the exact same circumstances but used Supernal magic, it would *still* trigger Dissonance in the person/people watching.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they weren\u2019t Sleepwalkers, which the practitioners of hoodoo (If it\u2019s working for them) would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:47:50-08:00","id":1179661,"title":"","content":"The Free Council will be more open to ideas of magic originating from things that have nothing to do with the Supernal, while the Diamond (and the Seers) will insist on the contrary. That Sleepwalker practitioner who argued with the Mystagogue will find an ear willing to listen among the Libertines. <br /> <br /> As you already suspect, it\u2019ll be an ST call. IIRC, the 2E materials haven\u2019t yet given us how common non-Supernal magic is supposed to be. We only know that Supernal magic is rare, and it doesn\u2019t seem so only because we\u2019re seeing things from the mages\u2019 perspectives. <br /> <br /> While \u201cfolk magic\u201d practitioners can be indeed Sleepwalkers, it\u2019s also entirely possible that a lot of those practices are actually just how the world in CoD functions, requiring no internal supernatural ability on part of those who exploit it. Like how anyone can do Abjurations, Exorcisms and the like.<br /> <br /> For now the only impact of altering the degree of Sleepwalker presence in the world that I can think of is how much the Awakened are alienated from the world, which would set the mood of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:49:22-08:00","id":1179662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179660#post1179660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if they weren\u2019t Sleepwalkers, which the practitioners of hoodoo (If it\u2019s working for them) would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, I'm assuming we're talking Sleepers if we're talking Dissonance. If the onlookers are sleepwalkers it's as fine and real to them as anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:54:43-08:00","id":1179663,"title":"","content":"So what I gather from this is that mage sight is inherent to humanity and sleepers just aren't able to process the symbols they see due to the shard of the abyss within them? Or maybe just because of The Lie. Otherwise seeing magic in a way perfectly compatible to their worldview wouldn't affect them so traumatically.<br /> <br /> Also, they've confirmed the two Arcadia's aren't the same? When was this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T17:01:38-08:00","id":1179665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonchild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179663#post1179663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, they've confirmed the two Arcadia's aren't the same? When was this?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/872952-a-changeling-related-question?p=872954#post872954\">Several times.</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T17:21:25-08:00","id":1179672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonchild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179663#post1179663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what I gather from this is that mage sight is inherent to humanity and sleepers just aren't able to process the symbols they see due to the shard of the abyss within them? Or maybe just because of The Lie. Otherwise seeing magic in a way perfectly compatible to their worldview wouldn't affect them so traumatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Mage Sight isn\u2019t inherent to humanity, it\u2019s inherent to Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T17:22:32-08:00","id":1179673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonchild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179663#post1179663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what I gather from this is that mage sight is inherent to humanity and sleepers just aren't able to process the symbols they see due to the shard of the abyss within them? Or maybe just because of The Lie. Otherwise seeing magic in a way perfectly compatible to their worldview wouldn't affect them so traumatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>The default state of humanity prior to the Sleeping Curse is Sleepwalker. (Remember the developer saying that, but can\u2019t recall where) So technically, Mage Sight is still unique to mages, and non-Awakened would still be unable to process Supernal symbols. It just doesn\u2019t fry their minds when they see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T17:26:35-08:00","id":1179676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179672#post1179672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, Mage Sight isn\u2019t inherent to humanity, it\u2019s inherent to Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go by the idea that being Awakened is the natural state of humanity but is blocked by the abyssal shard, you could argue that it was meant to be this way before The Fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","name":"GreenKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23750_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T17:30:15-08:00","id":1179678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreenKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179676#post1179676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you go by the idea that being Awakened is the natural state of humanity but is blocked by the abyssal shard, you could argue that it was meant to be this way before The Fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, being Awakened isn\u2019t the natural state of humanity, being a Sleepwalker is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T18:03:18-08:00","id":1179683,"title":"","content":"That's the leading theory of the Diamond and Seers, at any rate. Which can't actually be proven. As far as history is concerned, the world has always been Fallen (as seen in Sundered World). Quiescence, as I understand it, reacts specifically to Supernal magic alone... which now that I think about it may have been the basis for the idea that the Exarchs are not just another set of Supernal symbols but a group of ancient Ascended mages; that there's a higher, guiding intelligence actively behind whatever prevents mages from practicing their magic openly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T18:19:55-08:00","id":1179685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179683#post1179683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the leading theory of the Diamond and Seers, at any rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually the word from Dave. Although, I don't think it ever officially makes it into a book in such blunt terms. It can be taken as heavily implied though since regular people suffer Breaking Points from exposure to the supernatural (And the Supernal in particular), but Sleepwalkers don't when paired with the fact that Mages -are- monsters in the view of the authors because that's the way the CoD splat books are written to be taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T18:22:20-08:00","id":1179686,"title":"","content":"And said word is here:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/392-addicted-to-mystery-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-fallen-world-chronicles?p=177803#post177803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing is that in the current edition whether or not you forget depends on your willpower, with Willpower 9 or 10 Sleepers being able to remember magic.<br /> <br /> That's going away. They all forget.<br /> <br /> And yes, everyone in Second Sight or with one of the supernatural Merits in God Machine is meant to be a Sleepwalker. Being a Sleepwalker is the &amp;quot;natural&amp;quot; state of humanity, pre-Fall; not under the Curse, but not Awakened.<br /> <br /> It's also strictly speaking <i>worse</i> to be a Sleepwalker than a Sleeper. Because those Hunters who are Sleepwalkers? Mages can cast permenant spells on them without fear of Paradox. Do it to a Sleeper and eventually they'll unravel the spell. Being a Sleepwalker who isn't under the protection of mage society is like wearing an &amp;quot;kick me&amp;quot; sign.<br /> <br /> Which is why, if &amp;quot;is a Sleepwalker with no powers&amp;quot; is a Merit, it's going to be a <i>very</i> cheap one.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T18:50:22-08:00","id":1179690,"title":"","content":"If being a Sleepwalker is the natural state, I certainly got the wrong impression from the 2e book, which I got the impression that since the world is a &quot;Lie&quot;, and the Awakened are those who see how the world really works and past the Lie, and the Lie was put up after The Fall, then being Awakened was the natural state. Of course there is the idea that the Exarchs made it so because they can screw reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","user":"GreenKitty","date":". 01-26-2018, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","name":"GreenKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23750_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T19:02:42-08:00","id":1179695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreenKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179690#post1179690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If being a Sleepwalker is the natural state, I certainly got the wrong impression from the 2e book, which I got the impression that since the world is a &quot;Lie&quot;, and the Awakened are those who see how the world really works and past the Lie, and the Lie was put up after The Fall, then being Awakened was the natural state. Of course there is the idea that the Exarchs made it so because they can screw reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something you should realize is that the Awakened realize in a transcendental experience that the world is a Lie, and then the experience is over, and they're back in the Lie. And, the Lie is in some ways -really- fucking subtle, and Mages manage to tangle themselves back up in it again on those subtler levels even though they think they're looking out for it. Awakening is not an escape from the Lie. Ascension arguably is, but considering the reality edits and how that probably screws up the Supernal everytime it happens, who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T20:28:58-08:00","id":1179712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreenKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179690#post1179690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If being a Sleepwalker is the natural state, I certainly got the wrong impression from the 2e book, which I got the impression that since the world is a &amp;quot;Lie&amp;quot;, and the Awakened are those who see how the world really works and past the Lie, and the Lie was put up after The Fall, then being Awakened was the natural state. Of course there is the idea that the Exarchs made it so because they can screw reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, here\u2019s how I understand it: first, let\u2019s say that the Truth (of the Supernal) is fire, as that\u2019s a common analogy. <br /> <br /> Sleepwalkers are those who see an open fire, and while they recognize its dangers, they realize it can be also of help. <br /> <br /> Sleepers see the fire and are cowed like wild animals, seeing it only as something to be feared, running away from first sight. <br /> <br /> The Awakened are those enthralled by the fire. Some create torches to carry around the fire, lighting up the dark and banishing the cold. Some set things on fire to see how the tongues of flame dance, other people\u2019s fears be damned. Some plunge their hands into the fire, their own pain be damned. <br /> <br /> The Ascended are fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T20:42:50-08:00","id":1179715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179672#post1179672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, Mage Sight isn\u2019t inherent to humanity, it\u2019s inherent to Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, what I said was very poorly worded, and I later realized that.<br /> <br /> What I probably should have said was that if sleepers can look at a spell being cast in a way that perfectly melds with their worldview but still experience dissonance, then it seems like everyone must perceive the supernal to some degree. Otherwise it would be odd for just witnessing it to cause them, and the spell so much trouble.<br /> <br /> I wound up conflating any limited perception of the supernal at all with Mage sight, which in retrospect is probably like confusing a human sense of smell with a dog's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T20:56:51-08:00","id":1179718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonchild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179715#post1179715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, what I said was very poorly worded, and I later realized that.<br /> <br /> What I probably should have said was that if sleepers can look at a spell being cast in a way that perfectly melds with their worldview but still experience dissonance, then it seems like everyone must perceive the supernal to some degree. Otherwise it would be odd for just witnessing it to cause them, and the spell so much trouble.<br /> <br /> I wound up conflating any limited perception of the supernal at all with Mage sight, which in retrospect is probably like confusing a human sense of smell with a dog's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, furthermore there are plenty of spells that simply aren't &quot;visible&quot; to normal human senses. You manipulate something in twilight or the Shadow, yeah, good luck with perceiving that without magic. So technically you can actually use magic in front of sleepers. However, if they are in any way capable of perceiving your spell work (and I don't mean the use of yantras), then they're going to have to deal with dissonance and you're going to have to deal with paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T23:53:01-08:00","id":1179768,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Lie isn't (just) the Sleeping Curse; the Lie is the systems that exist to distract, mislead, and prevent humanity from grasping its divine heritage. It's the systems of control the Exarchs placed in the world to keep you downtrodden, but which also make you step on the necks of others.<br /> <br /> When hunger grips at empty bellies that could be full, and draws minds that should be free to base concerns, that is the Lie.<br /> <br /> When the Sleeping masses seek connection to the Truth and flock to hear spiritual teachers, sham occultists, and half-truthed materialists for succor, that is the Lie.<br /> <br /> When people must struggle for daily survival, clawing at one another in an unceasing competition that turns society into a pyramid, blazing with Exarchial sympathies, that is the Lie.<br /> <br /> The Awakened are no more free of it than most; the Duel Arcane itself is a paean to the General by its very nature.<br /> <br /> The Sleeping Curse, in 1e, manifested differently in cultures with a strong belief in magic; they might remember the magic, but reshape it to fit an evil narrative. I.E. Devout Christians might recall it as the work of devils. In 2e, that is no longer the case, but you're free to tweak it that way if you think it best for your games. RAW, though, everyone forgets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T03:06:42-08:00","id":1179781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179768#post1179768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Lie isn't (just) the Sleeping Curse; the Lie is the systems that exist to distract, mislead, and prevent humanity from grasping its divine heritage. It's the systems of control the Exarchs placed in the world to keep you downtrodden, but which also make you step on the necks of others.<br /> <br /> When hunger grips at empty bellies that could be full, and draws minds that should be free to base concerns, that is the Lie.<br /> <br /> When the Sleeping masses seek connection to the Truth and flock to hear spiritual teachers, sham occultists, and half-truthed materialists for succor, that is the Lie.<br /> <br /> When people must struggle for daily survival, clawing at one another in an unceasing competition that turns society into a pyramid, blazing with Exarchial sympathies, that is the Lie.<br /> <br /> The Awakened are no more free of it than most; the Duel Arcane itself is a paean to the General by its very nature.<br /> <br /> The Sleeping Curse, in 1e, manifested differently in cultures with a strong belief in magic; they might remember the magic, but reshape it to fit an evil narrative. I.E. Devout Christians might recall it as the work of devils. In 2e, that is no longer the case, but you're free to tweak it that way if you think it best for your games. RAW, though, everyone forgets.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my games I would have it work more like this, that much of the beliefs people have are part of the Lie to distractbfrom Truth. And the Lie is an active suppressor that say, causes Youtube videos of actual summoning to paradox into disaster. <br /> <br /> Yet it contradicts the idea that such beliefs do contain &quot;The Truth&quot;, and I could see your explanation being presented by Diamond Order dogmatists and then a Libertine pops up and says that these aspects of the Lie contain functioning &quot;Truth&quot; and then an ideological brawl occurs. <br /> <br /> When something like this is presented in very asbstract terms, it can be interpreted in a lot of ways, leaving the ST freedom to change them. Yet, in-character ot would seem like everything is couched in so much symbolism and since mages think everything is symbols, maybe everyone ends up deriving a multitude of &quot;Truths&quot; from them, even &quot;alternative truth&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . <br /> <br /> So anyway what else I am getting here is that before The Fall, humans could have the freedom to Awaken if they wished to and there was no Paradox to stop mages from instantly zapping anyone in front of them or using space arcanum to kidnap children. <br /> <br /> However it would suggest that back in &quot;Atlantis&quot;(or the age of) even &quot;Sleepwalkers&quot; would be born into a &quot;Lie&quot; that is the world because they cannot see the Supernal infrastructure of the world. So therefore at least this aspect of &quot;Lie&quot; is always present since the beginning; furthermore due to not wanting to cross splats, it would be impossible for a vampire to Awaken and therefore all other supernaturals are doomed to never Awaken&quot;l due to some taint or imbalance in the soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","user":"GreenKitty","date":". 01-27-2018, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","name":"GreenKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23750_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T04:03:53-08:00","id":1179790,"title":"","content":"I gotta dispute the claims that its not affected by belief. It most certainly, canonically is.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Curse strikes a Sleeper when she sees obvious<br /> magic, either during the spell\u2019s casting or<br /> encountering its effects later. So what\u2019s obvious?<br /> The spell must be clearly, openly supernatural in<br /> effect, and the Sleeper must be both conscious<br /> and cognizant of the magic\u2019s impossibility.&quot;<br /> <br /> In other words, while ancient mages did struggle with Quiescence, different cultures and perspectives are going to have somewhat different viewpoints on what is possible and impossible and what is supernatural and not supernatural. Technology, for example, radically redefines the nature of possible and impossible. Culture and belief systems DO play a huge part, and modern people aren't always more skeptical of magic.<br /> <br /> The impossibility of zombies and robots, for example, is fairly variable.<br /> <br /> &quot;Conscious and cognizant of the magic's impossibility&quot; is another essential part. If you send obvious zombies walking down the street, that's probably going to be something that is clearly, openly supernatural that people will be conscious and cognizant of it being impossible. If these people are in the middle of a (non-magic related) zombie apocalypse, they blatantly know zombies are possible and they sure as hell aren't going to know which zombies are possible and which are impossible, which are made by an improbable disease and which is made by magic. If the zombies are relatively lifelike, they may never be recognized as supernatural to begin with; it may very well be a riot of stinking, drugged, mentally ill persons. If the sleepers don't know they were made by magic, even if someone fully well knows they're zombies, its not altogether clear how impossible that is that something could cause zombie like phenomena. And even if its a hunter who fully well knows that a mage is responsible somehow, unless he saw a dead body rise, its just as possible that these are diseased people who can be cured, laboring under a curse. Meanwhile, an empty, walking skeleton is almost always going to draw the Curse, even if non-mage created skeletons have been wandering around; they're clearly supernatural, and you can just plainly see it. An angry decapitated head rolling after you, biting your toes or otherwise truly surreal looking zombies almost certainly draws the Curse too.<br /> <br /> A robot (golem) walking down the street? If it looks human enough to not draw suspicion, no Curse. If it is boxy enough to possibly have a human in there somewhere, that remains a possibility; no Curse. If the Statue of Liberty comes to life like Talos, sure, but even if someone is familiar with the limits of humanoid robots, and a viewer gasps with astonishment to see such an agile, realistic, and lively robot dancing for his amusement, and it strains belief far beyond what he thinks is possible; its still probably not not *clearly and openly* supernatural. Meanwhile, ancient people are much more likely to go &quot;Oh yeah... that's magic, alright.&quot; The robot IS impossible; its apparent workings are just for show, it has no power source and the technology for it doesn't exist yet. The ancient doesn't know WHY its impossible; just that it is. Bam, Curse.<br /> <br /> And its even more complicated than that!<br /> <br /> To a modern person, the vast gulf between a dragon and an alligator seems obvious -- but then again, plenty of people believe in aliens and cryptids. To the people who wrote medieval bestiaries, the line between real and unreal is much more blurry. To an ancient who already lives with an honest to goodness (non mage related) dragon, a mage's spell-born dragon may just be a normal animal; he is neither conscious nor cognizant of the dragon's impossibility. The dragon IS supernatural, but its supernatural nature is not necessarily clear, nor is the ancient one cognizant of that impossibility.<br /> <br /> What about an elephant?<br /> <br /> Its the opposite of the robot scenario. To that same ignorant ancient, a mage's spell-born elephant may very well BE something he thinks is completely impossible, but an elephant is, itself, not impossible. Nobody knows its not possible, but an elephant conjured by magic roaming about where sleepers who don't know that elephants exist is probably not going to trigger the Curse unless its genesis was clearly supernatural.<br /> <br /> So what's pretty interesting about this is -- if a sleeper believes in and is 100% used to magic, and he knows you're using magic or miracles, Curse. The Lie is much more finetuned than owod Consensus; the sort of stuff that is considered &quot;objectively impossible&quot; by the Lie ultimately centers around humans awakening to the ability of drawing down transcendental powers. That's why folk awakened who pose as, or are, folk magicians and willworkers hit people with the Curse, and why impersonal weird things are much more mutable. The Curse isn't about necessarily believing in an ordered world of logical physics (the ancients often didn't); the Curse is about keeping sleepers from becoming mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T05:26:25-08:00","id":1179798,"title":"","content":"This thread seems to have wandered off course, and I'll happily admit I haven't read the whole thing.<br /> <br /> OP, to answer your question - it still works normally. Reference Dark Eras (Neolithic) where we have an entire society that's well aware that magic is real, it's a cornerstone of their culture and they struggle with and against it every day.<br /> <br /> Quiescence still works normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T09:43:31-08:00","id":1179858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreenKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179781#post1179781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet it contradicts the idea that such beliefs do contain &quot;The Truth&quot;, and I could see your explanation being presented by Diamond Order dogmatists and then a Libertine pops up and says that these aspects of the Lie contain functioning &quot;Truth&quot; and then an ideological brawl occurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing about the presence of the Lie denies the presence of Truth, any more than a distortion in a mirror or noise in a signal means that they contain nothing of what they reflect or transmit. The Lie is a distraction from the knowledge of higher reality; a disruption of a truer reading. It's not a complete disconnect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T13:23:48-08:00","id":1179919,"title":"","content":"The basic difference between a Sleeper and a Sleepwalker is that the Sleeper has a piece of the Abyss in their soul, the Sleepwalker doesn't.<br /> \u200bA Sleeper may not recognize the difference between just plain old supernatural and the Supernal but the Abyss does, it recognizes Supernal magic when it sees it and reacts regardless of the beliefs of the Sleeper.<br /> \u200bThat Abyssal shard is, however, dependent upon the senses of the Sleeper so if the Sleeper's senses don't see the Supernal at work neither does the Abyss and therefore there is no Dissonance.<br /> \u200bThis means that if the Sleeper lives in a culture where non Supernal magic is common and he doesn't see the actual casting of the spell, both he and that Abyssal shard can easily believe that the fruit of that spell came from something else and there is no Dissonance.<br /> \u200bSo long as a Mage in such a culture hides his actual Supernal casting from the senses of the Sleepers around him everything is good. He doesn't have to worry about the two stones he just stacked atop each other with magic falling down the first time his Sleeper neighbors see them.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn the Time Before, if such a time ever actually existed, there was no Abyss, no Abyssal shards and thus, no Sleepers. Everyone was by default then a Sleepwalker with the Awakened being those who had taken the step of creating a sympathetic link to the Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 01-27-2018, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T18:01:43-08:00","id":1179996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179790#post1179790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotta dispute the claims that its not affected by belief. It most certainly, canonically is.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Curse strikes a Sleeper when she sees obvious<br /> magic, either during the spell\u2019s casting or<br /> encountering its effects later. So what\u2019s obvious?<br /> The spell must be clearly, openly supernatural in<br /> effect, and the Sleeper must be both conscious<br /> and cognizant of the magic\u2019s impossibility.&quot;<br /> <br /> In other words, while ancient mages did struggle with Quiescence, different cultures and perspectives are going to have somewhat different viewpoints on what is possible and impossible and what is supernatural and not supernatural. Technology, for example, radically redefines the nature of possible and impossible. Culture and belief systems DO play a huge part, and modern people aren't always more skeptical of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read that part as Quiescence being shaped by <i>perception</i>, not belief. After all, we aren't talking about Ascension here, where Reality Zones and Paradigms and subjective truths are a thing. The Diamond and the Free Council aren't working on different Paradigms that make their magic work differently. Even Libertines accept that magic comes from the Supernal, and not directly from Sleeper culture they are invested in. They instead believe that Sleeper culture as a whole can change how Supernal symbols interact with the Fallen World. As Below, So Above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T18:19:49-08:00","id":1180001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179919#post1179919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic difference between a Sleeper and a Sleepwalker is that the Sleeper has a piece of the Abyss in their soul, the Sleepwalker doesn't.<br /> \u200bA Sleeper may not recognize the difference between just plain old supernatural and the Supernal but the Abyss does, it recognizes Supernal magic when it sees it and reacts regardless of the beliefs of the Sleeper.<br /> \u200bThat Abyssal shard is, however, dependent upon the senses of the Sleeper so if the Sleeper's senses don't see the Supernal at work neither does the Abyss and therefore there is no Dissonance...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the way I understand it. It's not important what the Sleeper believes, but what the Abyss perceives. However, I would clarify that a Sleeper doesn't have to recognize it as Supernal themselves to trigger paradox. It's not &quot;that must be Supernal magic, as opposed to regular magic, which I believe in&quot; that's required.<br /> <br /> The way I run it, it's specifically the &quot;this can't be happening!&quot; reaction that draws the Abyss' attention, even if the phenomenon fits a Sleeper's worldview or could otherwise be rationalized later. Thus, even if a given Sleeper believes in aliens, if a supernal UFO suddenly lands on their front lawn, all it takes is that moment of the Sleeper disbelieving their senses for the abyss to take notice and slip through. (By contrast, a person accustomed to personal visits from aliens wouldn't <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">immediately </span>trigger dissonance if a mage were to <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">counterfeit </span>one with Supernal magic.)<br /> <br /> To give a less extreme example, it's perfectly possible by modern science (if improbable) to spontaneously loose feeling in both legs and vision in one eye, but most people are still going to experience a moment of disbelief, and bam, dissonance (yes, I have a player who has Exceptional Luck as a rote, why do you ask?). To wit: it's &quot;Sleepers witnessing an obvious manifestation of the Supernal&quot; (pg. 298) not &quot;Sleepers witnessing an obviously Supernal manifestation&quot;.<br /> <br /> In short, at least in my games, you can't cheese your way out of paradox/dissonance when using &quot;vulgar&quot; magic just because it could be explained <i>after</i> the fact. It might be harsher than the way some people run it, but I found nothing beats ruining a character's power trip than rolling a critical success on those sweet, sweet paradox dice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. (Let's just say that Acanthus will think twice before he hexes an entire room full of Sleepers again.)<br /> <br /> Edit: felt like I would more directly address the OP. From my position, a society that believes in magic would certainly let a mage get away with more, but unless the people are actually experiencing the supernatural on a regular basis, most obvious supernal magic will still suffer dissonance because it's not &quot;normal&quot;. I would also keep in mind that it's pretty common for &quot;magic users&quot; to be pushed to the edges of society (not necessarily shunned, but certainly kept &quot;apart&quot;) even in cultures that have them as part of them belief system. Even if you belief in it, magic is still &quot;the weird stuff we don't understand&quot;, and watching the village wizard summon time-demons from Arcadia will still break your brain. Again, it's less about belief and more about Cthuloid horrors trying to break into reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 01-27-2018, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T19:03:41-08:00","id":1180011,"title":"","content":"I think the crux of what I'm really asking about is if exposure to the supernatural causes Sleepers to become Sleepwalkers. Some things hint it does, but if it does then, theoretically you could have large populations of Sleepwalkers in cultures that believe in the supernatural.<br /> <br /> So I'm going to do my best to explain what I am asking about, even if it seems the answer is obvious.<br /> <br /> Okay so I'll put here this:<br /> <br /> Settlement A: In here, low magic practitioners do produce results because the supernatural is a huge part of the World of Darkness-spirits, ghosts, etc abound. These low magic practitioners are Sleepwalkers. Belief and sight of the results of these magic practitioners especially during ceremonies is common, so therefore almost all inhabitants are Sleepwalkers. An Awakened here suffers little Paradox when casting, even to Sleepwalkers who <b>will accept Supernal practices as part of the craft, but they don't fully comprehend them, such as incorporation of High Speech phrases in prayers</b>, however it's possible that Paradox is still watching, so most of the time the Awakened here will hide most of their Supernal aspects of their work to others, hence many rituals are done in private and there are strong taboos about who can and cannot witness a specific ceremony.<br /> <br /> Settlement B: In here, the Awakened are shunned as possessed, witches, or other disgraced magic users while low magic users are seen as the proper magic users according to their beliefs. Here, the exposure to the supernatural does not cause Sleepers to become Sleepwalkers, but instead causes them to shun the Awakened, perhaps the reason involves Acamoths and Gulmoths.<br /> <br /> Settlement C: Here, exposure to the supernatural does not remove the Abyssal shard, so Awakened still have to practice away from the rest of their community, or maybe they can do it to some (Sleepwalkers), but not to others (Sleepers). Belief in magic <i><b>and</b></i> exposure to the supernatural alone does not remove the Abyssal shard, instead one has to be actively involved in it for a long time, hence the person who talks to spirits is a Sleepwalker. Yet this would assume that involvement with the supernatural is not an everyday practice for everyone, perhaps this is real difference between Settlement C and Settlement A. Or maybe all involvement with the supernatural is just fake and the darker mysteries of the World of Darkness leave these people alone.<br /> <br /> Settlement D: The conditions here are identical to Settlement A, except is that Awakened have to hide at least the obviously Supernal aspects of their work. Quiescence merely makes it easier for people to think of Awakened magic, as well as symbols and High Speech as parts of low magic, unless somehow it is impossible by their wide breadth of belief in the supernatural. However, it's unclear what separates Sleeper and Sleepwalker from the outside as both would be nearly identical.<br /> <br /> So which settlement would be &quot;correct&quot;? Or maybe all four would be depending on certain circumstances.<br /> <br /> I don't have access to the Sundered World Dark Eras book, but would that be Settlement B?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","user":"GreenKitty","date":". 01-28-2018, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","name":"GreenKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23750_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T21:01:59-08:00","id":1180052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179996#post1179996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read that part as Quiescence being shaped by <i>perception</i>, not belief. After all, we aren't talking about Ascension here, where Reality Zones and Paradigms and subjective truths are a thing. .</div> </div> </div> </div>There are definitely not subjective truths (mage related ones anyway), but there definitely are subjective lies. One of the few (ambiguously) positive elements mentioned in Seers of the Throne is the writeup of the Corrupt Medic; that a legitimate form of Seer character is a super doctor, who tricks people into thinking they've been healed with radical medical practices when in reality she's using healing magic. They aren't above inflicting diseases that they later cure to reinforce that Doctor Knows Best of course. There is definitely a strong element of belief there. As a side note, the medical industry fits the feel of the Seers even more than it did the Technocracy; medical professionals often intentionally or unintentionally cultivate an air of mysterious, unquestioned authority and hidden lore with their weird symbols and their latin.<br /> <br /> Another archetypal Seer character mentioned is the Investigator of Miracles; an apparent priest who goes around investigating and respectfully explaining away miracles, taking over the rare, genuinely miraculous sites; and, if they are not miracles from the Seers, they will be sanitized into mundanity. This, too, definitely involves belief.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1179996#post1179996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Diamond and the Free Council aren't working on different Paradigms that make their magic work differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Free Council most definitely does engage in (little p) paradigm engineering with sleepers. They do indeed monkey around with what people believe is possible and impossible. The Free Council, like the Guardians of the Veil, do sometimes find themselves becoming so obsessed that they act in ironic common cause with Seers and even nudging people away from Awakening on purpose. There are Libertines who try to push the boundaries of real scientific research, Libertines who make enhanced tech gadgets and &quot;fake tech&quot; (using spells to do as tech did but better, like making &quot;better robots&quot; and &quot;better flamethrowers&quot; and so forth), and Libertines that try to make sleepers just plain accept a wider range of possibilities. Libertines don't suddenly start thinking they're just gifted boffins a la some confused owod technomancer, but different Libertines definitely vary on what the borders of acceptability, possibility and probability are. In terms of owod analogies, some techy Libertines are more like technomancers with pet scientific theories and all, and some are almost totally ignorant regarding science and just use technology as special effects props.<br /> <br /> Paradigms are inward and outward focused in MtAsc, but while inward facing (lower case) paradigms have little effect in Awakening, mages most certainly do present themselves as boffins, miracle workers, wise women, and extreme martial artists to give sleepers different ways to relate to their magic (if they're not totally secretive at all times), and boffins and extreme martial artists do indeed work slightly differently even though they are (hopefully) totally aware of what they're doing. The Guardians, on the other hand, definitely trick themselves almost as much as they trick anyone else.<br /> <br /> One of the big charms of Awakening for me (someone who grew up with Ascension) is that instead of it being mostly subjectivity (with some objective elements that mages usually aggressively ignore), its two objective realities (the Supernal and Phenomenal Worlds) sandwiching an anti-reality (the Abyss) with the vagaries of mages, sleepwalkers, sleepers and the Lie, and different levels of reality-ness and fallen-ness (verges, demenses, a mage in his private dream world vs a sleeper in his with mage guests, etc). What is particularly curious is that in the most &quot;subjective reality&quot; possible, his own personal dream world, a mage suffers no paradox at all, while even though while you're asleep you would logically not be able to even be able to begin to understand the borders of natural and supernatural, a sleeper's Oneiros is automatically cognizant of all magic transpiring inside as traumatizing, impossible, and supernatural. Apropos of Inception, I suppose.<br /> <br /> But if you don't think the level of cognizance of the supernatural and the impossible fits Awakening's themes pertaining to whether sleepers are affected by the Curse, the dictionary definition of cognizance includes: &quot;awareness, realization, or knowledge; notice; perception.&quot; There is a distinct &quot;eureka!&quot; moment associated with the Quiescence, as it is described as a botched awakening. The Lie isn't there to keep people from believing in weird stuff, its there to keep people from awakening, and its there to keep the awakened and Supernal beings on their toes, with some weird stuff being prohibited as a side effect.<br /> <br /> Finally, its worth pointing out that 1e-&gt;2e radically changed these elements: stuff is just plain vulgar or covert in 1e with no appeals process allowed (except for the worse), while in 2e sleeper reactions are almost an afterthought and the main cause of problems is reaching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T21:13:29-08:00","id":1180057,"title":"","content":"I default to C, though I could see it varying between B and D given different circumstances. I haven't actually read Sundered Worlds, but my understanding was that it was somewhere around D: people know mages are a thing, but the Awakened have to keep their cool toys behind the curtain so as to not break peoples' minds. Take that for what you will <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> As for how Sleepwalkers start...sleepwalking? My understanding was that exposure to the supernatural was strongly correlated with sleepwalking, but that it was still up in the air if a given individual would become one or not, and some people are sleepwalkers for no discernible reason. And sometimes it's maybe sorta hereditary. Basically it's set up without hard and fast rules so the storyteller can do what they want. Which is not very helpful if you're the kind of storyteller that likes the setting to have well-defined rules *cough*. Personally, I would say that you would only get a village of sleepwalkers under very exceptional circumstances, but I do prefer to keep supernal magic rare and weird, especially if low magic is common. Dunno if that helps at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T21:18:13-08:00","id":1180060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1180052#post1180052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are definitely not subjective truths (mage related ones anyway), but there definitely are subjective lies. One of the few (ambiguously) positive elements mentioned in Seers of the Throne is the writeup of the Corrupt Medic; that a legitimate form of Seer character is a super doctor, who tricks people into thinking they've been healed with radical medical practices when in reality she's using healing magic. They aren't above inflicting diseases that they later cure to reinforce that Doctor Knows Best of course. There is definitely a strong element of belief there. As a side note, the medical industry fits the feel of the Seers even more than it did the Technocracy; medical professionals often intentionally or unintentionally cultivate an air of mysterious, unquestioned authority and hidden lore with their weird symbols and their latin.<br /> <br /> Another archetypal Seer character mentioned is the Investigator of Miracles; an apparent priest who goes around investigating and respectfully explaining away miracles, taking over the rare, genuinely miraculous sites; and, if they are not miracles from the Seers, they will be sanitized into mundanity. This, too, definitely involves belief.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, true, but these are Seers we're talking about. It's less about belief shaping how magic works, and more about the guys doing magic having their own beliefs on what they should do with magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Free Council most definitely does engage in (little p) paradigm engineering with sleepers. They do indeed monkey around with what people believe is possible and impossible. The Free Council, like the Guardians of the Veil, do sometimes find themselves becoming so obsessed that they act in ironic common cause with Seers and even nudging people away from Awakening on purpose. There are Libertines who try to push the boundaries of real scientific research, Libertines who make enhanced tech gadgets and &quot;fake tech&quot; (using spells to do as tech did but better, like making &quot;better robots&quot; and &quot;better flamethrowers&quot; and so forth), and Libertines that try to make sleepers just plain accept a wider range of possibilities. Libertines don't suddenly start thinking they're just gifted boffins a la some confused owod technomancer, but different Libertines definitely vary on what the borders of acceptability, possibility and probability are. In terms of owod analogies, some techy Libertines are more like technomancers with pet scientific theories and all, and some are almost totally ignorant regarding science and just use technology as special effects props.<br /> <br /> Paradigms are inward and outward focused in MtAsc, but while inward facing (lower case) paradigms have little effect in Awakening, mages most certainly do present themselves as boffins, miracle workers, wise women, and extreme martial artists to give sleepers different ways to relate to their magic (if they're not totally secretive at all times), and boffins and extreme martial artists do indeed work slightly differently even though they are (hopefully) totally aware of what they're doing. The Guardians, on the other hand, definitely trick themselves almost as much as they trick anyone else. </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, mages are still people, and people hold onto their own private beliefs and paradigms, and such things will certainly affect how they perceive themselves and how they will be inclined to use their magic. I was only arguing against capital-P Paradigms, where those personal beliefs and lowercase-p paradigms actually change how magic works.<br /> <br /> Granted, it does seem like we're splitting hairs, because...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if you don't think the level of cognizance of the supernatural and the impossible fits Awakening's themes pertaining to whether sleepers are affected by the Curse, the dictionary definition of cognizance includes: &quot;awareness, realization, or knowledge; notice; perception.&quot; There is a distinct &quot;eureka!&quot; moment associated with the Quiescence, as it is described as a botched awakening. The Lie isn't there to keep people from believing in weird stuff, its there to keep people from awakening, and its there to keep the awakened and Supernal beings on their toes, with some weird stuff being prohibited as a side effect. </div> </div> </div>... I actually agree with this conclusion. Communication failure from vocabulary, I think? Belief and perception, subjectivity and objectivity, etc. Pretty heavy concepts, now that I look at it. (And one I imagine in-universe characters have to deal with every time!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T21:46:11-08:00","id":1180065,"title":"","content":"&quot;I don't have access to the Sundered World Dark Eras book, but would that be Settlement B?&quot;<br /> <br /> Neolithic mages with fully believing sleeper friends have to do the overtly supernatural elements of their craft in private (ie. magicking up furrows for an irrigation canal that would have taken all the men in the village busy for months), but they can display the finished product in public afterwards, and they can do the yantras with the complete knowledge and intent of the town that, yes, he's doing magic and that, yes, the ditches were made by magic. Yes, the tattoo I gave you while you were sedated gives you extra health and luck.<br /> <br /> Although sleepwalkers are not a particularly important part of the sample Neolithic setting and not particularly prevalent (if the Wise are thought of as &quot;fire bearers&quot; then the Wise think of sleepwalkers as &quot;ember bearers,&quot; and there's not really any further attention given to them), even sleepers make use of extensive rituals and ceremonies to protect themselves from spirits, to placate and sacrifice to spirits, and so forth. You can actually, knowingly, make sacrificial pots for mages to use as yantras every day, in a village whose building you know was magicked into existence (while noone was watching) by a mage, help a mage perform his yantras, and then say goodbye to the mage who you helped with yantras who tells you &quot;Ok, I'm going to go into the sacred hut to finish my obvious magic, bye&quot; and not be a sleepwalker. It seems to be less belief and more partial magic use.<br /> <br /> Its ironic that mages derive fabulous benefits from sleepwalker assistance (a mage in a village comprised of 100 sleepwalkers he's friends with could potentially get 100 extra spells) but they have a hard time directly making them directly, while other monsters sometimes make them in bulk.<br /> <br /> Also, I can't find any evidence that monsters are themselves sleepwalkers -- it seems to be &quot;integrity + supernatural merit reflecting innate capability/minor template/sleepwalker merit/etc.&quot; Meaning, I don't think they can carry spells like a sleepwalker can.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T22:13:14-08:00","id":1180069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreenKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1180011#post1180011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the crux of what I'm really asking about is if exposure to the supernatural causes Sleepers to become Sleepwalkers. Some things hint it does, but if it does then, theoretically you could have large populations of Sleepwalkers in cultures that believe in the supernatural.<br /> <br /> So I'm going to do my best to explain what I am asking about, even if it seems the answer is obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is outright a merit to represent this. Importantly, though, as others have pointed out, being a Sleeper does not prevent you from believing in the supernatural or even actively engaging with it. A Sleeper can:<br /> <br /> -Summon, bind, and abjure ghosts and spirits<br /> -Wield magical relics<br /> -Commune with the above beings<br /> -Witness the use of Legacy attainments<br /> -Craft magical amulets<br /> <br /> And so on. All without forgetting or being a Sleepwalker.<br /> <br /> Does witnessing the supernatural often enough turn you into a Sleepwalker? No, not automatically or reliably. Plenty of people just break and go insane. But it can happen, and happens sufficiently often for the Awakened to recognize it. Mystery cults are founded on this premise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T06:01:28-08:00","id":1180138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreenKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1180011#post1180011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have access to the Sundered World Dark Eras book, but would that be Settlement B?</div> </div> </div> </div>Settlement C is the closest to what's presented there, however everyone in the setting <b>does</b> interact with the supernatural regularly (there is no Gauntlet, so Spirits are kind of everywhere).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T10:05:18-08:00","id":1180194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreenKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1180011#post1180011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the crux of what I'm really asking about is if exposure to the supernatural causes Sleepers to become Sleepwalkers. Some things hint it does, but if it does then, theoretically you could have large populations of Sleepwalkers in cultures that believe in the supernatural.<br /> <br /> So I'm going to do my best to explain what I am asking about, even if it seems the answer is obvious.<br /> <br /> Okay so I'll put here this:<br /> <br /> Settlement A: In here, low magic practitioners do produce results because the supernatural is a huge part of the World of Darkness-spirits, ghosts, etc abound. These low magic practitioners are Sleepwalkers. Belief and sight of the results of these magic practitioners especially during ceremonies is common, so therefore almost all inhabitants are Sleepwalkers. An Awakened here suffers little Paradox when casting, even to Sleepwalkers who <b>will accept Supernal practices as part of the craft, but they don't fully comprehend them, such as incorporation of High Speech phrases in prayers</b>, however it's possible that Paradox is still watching, so most of the time the Awakened here will hide most of their Supernal aspects of their work to others, hence many rituals are done in private and there are strong taboos about who can and cannot witness a specific ceremony.<br /> <br /> Settlement B: In here, the Awakened are shunned as possessed, witches, or other disgraced magic users while low magic users are seen as the proper magic users according to their beliefs. Here, the exposure to the supernatural does not cause Sleepers to become Sleepwalkers, but instead causes them to shun the Awakened, perhaps the reason involves Acamoths and Gulmoths.<br /> <br /> Settlement C: Here, exposure to the supernatural does not remove the Abyssal shard, so Awakened still have to practice away from the rest of their community, or maybe they can do it to some (Sleepwalkers), but not to others (Sleepers). Belief in magic <i><b>and</b></i> exposure to the supernatural alone does not remove the Abyssal shard, instead one has to be actively involved in it for a long time, hence the person who talks to spirits is a Sleepwalker. Yet this would assume that involvement with the supernatural is not an everyday practice for everyone, perhaps this is real difference between Settlement C and Settlement A. Or maybe all involvement with the supernatural is just fake and the darker mysteries of the World of Darkness leave these people alone.<br /> <br /> Settlement D: The conditions here are identical to Settlement A, except is that Awakened have to hide at least the obviously Supernal aspects of their work. Quiescence merely makes it easier for people to think of Awakened magic, as well as symbols and High Speech as parts of low magic, unless somehow it is impossible by their wide breadth of belief in the supernatural. However, it's unclear what separates Sleeper and Sleepwalker from the outside as both would be nearly identical.<br /> <br /> So which settlement would be &quot;correct&quot;? Or maybe all four would be depending on certain circumstances.<br /> <br /> I don't have access to the Sundered World Dark Eras book, but would that be Settlement B?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you say which supplements those are so we aren't guessing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T05:33:53-08:00","id":1181093,"title":"","content":"The thing about pre-Fall is a sticky thing, as (as far as mages can tell from trending themes in the mutually -exclusive relics of the Time Before they've found) Sleepers did not exist in that world... But neither did mages, or not as the Fallen World knows them. Most versions of pre-Fall &quot;mages&quot; gained their powers by meditating in demesnes, as pre-fall you could access the Supernal through the far end of the Anima Mundi, then claimed their powers in a personal Supernal space rather than use a Watchtower.<br /> <br /> they were, effectively, closer (but still not the same as) Fallen World *archmasters*, not mages.<br /> <br /> (&quot;but where did the demesnes come from for the first pre-fall people?&quot; Says the apprentice. &quot;Sariras&quot; says the thearch tutor, nodding safely.<br /> <br /> &quot;But hang on, a Sarira is the result of an Ascension. That's *less* possible than soul stones!&quot; Says the apprentice.<br /> <br /> &quot;Err... There must have been another race who awakened before humanity did but ascended rather than cause a Fall, and the first Atlanteans found their demesnes&quot; ventures the master<br /> <br /> &quot;and what were they like?&quot; Asks the apprentice.<br /> <br /> &quot;Dragons!&quot; Says the master, and the Atlantean Mythos is born.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T05:48:27-08:00","id":1181098,"title":"","content":"So, it's basically the prehistory of Faerum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T05:56:32-08:00","id":1181102,"title":"","content":"I love the prehistory of Abeir-Toril. Not many D&amp;D worlds say &quot;anything you can play? Immigrants. There's five native races, one of them's dragons, one of them's (bizarrely) doppelgangers.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T06:02:50-08:00","id":1181106,"title":"","content":"After seeing that, I now decide in my headcanon that the pre-Fall world is the world in Mage the Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T08:31:26-08:00","id":1181137,"title":"","content":"I like your semi-sarcastic descriptions, Dave; it makes me think of Father Ted but with wizards.<br /> <br /> &quot;So I hear you're Jnanamukti now, Hierophant.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What!? Who said I'm an Jnanamukti?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Everyone's saying it, Hierophant! Should we be all Jnanamukti now? What's the official line the Mysterium is taking?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No, no-!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Only, the Mysteries take up most of my time, and at night I just like a good book, so I might not be able to devote myself full-time to the genocide of Sleepers.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T13:27:37-08:00","id":1181209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1181102#post1181102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the prehistory of Abeir-Toril. Not many D&amp;D worlds say &quot;anything you can play? Immigrants. There's five native races, one of them's dragons, one of them's (bizarrely) doppelgangers.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those land stealing immigrants.<br /> <br /> Yeah, out of the Toril natives, most had scales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T14:03:43-08:00","id":1181226,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to say it was aliens. Maybe alien dragons. Maybe ascension turns people into alien dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23750-greenkitty","name":"GreenKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23750_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T14:18:15-08:00","id":1181229,"title":"","content":"Did pre-fall mages have to undergo the threshold seeking in order to access Imperial practices or were they as accessible as the regular practices?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T14:49:55-08:00","id":1181236,"title":"","content":"Even the dragon mythos is just exactly that; a myth. <br /> <br /> We do know that the whole precursors-as-dragons and magical dragons imagery was introduced by the Tremere, back when they were of the Diamond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T04:53:07-08:00","id":1182231,"title":"","content":"My favorite answer to the original question is:<br /> <br /> Quiescence works normally, but within the cultural expectations. That is, when it distorts the perceived effects it uses culturally-appropriate forms. The magic that they recall isn't supernal, anymore, which is the part that their soul rejects. The incorrect notions of magic are already acceptable to the Sleepers and what they believe is possible. Therefore, things that appear to be truly fitting their paradigm wouldn't be perceived to be impossible and prod that abyssal part of their souls. (and &quot;perceive&quot; not &quot;witness&quot; is the word used, IIRC)<br /> <br /> This could lead to a situation where a population realize that one witch talks a very different game than the rest, but <i>everybody</i> <i>knows</i> he's doing the same things. They've <b>seen </b>it. Forcing the discrimination would not be nice.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure, Bob, you're much more powerful than Mother Ida. Okay, man. Yeah, you touched the fury of the heavens or whatever. That's nice. Mind finishing up that luck charm for me? My wife's giving birth soon and I'd like her to have it during labor. Thanks. You're the best witch we have. I tell it to everybody.&quot;<br /> <br /> (And we <i>don't</i> <b>know</b> that the Tremere introduced any such thing. They simply claim to be the holders of the One True History; If that is suspect so's the rest.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 02-04-2018, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T09:18:35-08:00","id":1182285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1182231#post1182231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(And we <i>don't</i> <b>know</b> that the Tremere introduced any such thing. They simply claim to be the holders of the One True History; If that is suspect so's the rest.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave mentioned it sometime ago. If the Diamond aren't literal descendants of Atlantis, then you need to find a reason that they have this unified dragon motif. Presumably it'll actually get clearly laid down in Tome of the Pentacle whenever that appears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T09:33:13-08:00","id":1182290,"title":"","content":"I think it'll remain one of those out-of-book things unless the Tremere get a full write-up, and there it would be portrayed as a legend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1034137#post1034137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where exactly did you think the whole Dragon symbolism motif came from, anyway?<br /> <br /> (That's right! The Diamond got it from the Tremere!)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-04-2018, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T14:15:13-08:00","id":1182381,"title":"","content":"Way back when second edition was called &quot;Mystery Play: The Fallen World Chronicle&quot; and we were examining what we would change about the first edition's early books with benefit of hindsight, increasing the histiroicity of the Orders was big on our to-do list. The gameline hasn't ever been as &quot;Atlantis! Then nothing ever changes!&quot; as it's sometimes made out to be - the Mysterium being created from the Pancryptiates and Keepers by the Corpus Author, the Arrow abandoning mortal society after World War 2, the Nameless War and the Great Refusal are all in those early books, but we leant into it hard in second edition. So yeah, I know what the Fourth Great Ministry of Seers was before Panopticon took their place, and just as we showed in Dark Eras where the Diamond gets a lot of its terminology and beliefs from, we have taken the few centuries gap between the Tremere becoming liches and being found out and driven into hiding by the Diamond and made them a former Diamond Order. Part of that was deciding what of the modern Pentacle's beliefs traces back to them, and the Dragon won.<br /> <br /> A lot of Awakening's setting, in my tenure, has been &quot;this thing first ed said they believe. What evidence do they actually have for it, how did they arrive at that hypothesis, and when did it become accepted?&quot; Often using the language or mythology the words for things come from as a guide. Retrofitting the Awakened into being <i>competent</i> academics instead of just metaphors for them.<br /> <br /> Which is pertinent to the other thread going on at the moment, about challenging Supernal &quot;truth&quot;. First ed Mage was interested in telling you mages knew the truth. We're interested in showing you how and why they know it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T14:18:49-08:00","id":1182384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1182381#post1182381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Way back when second edition was called &quot;Mystery Play: The Fallen World Chronicle&quot; and we were examining what we would change about the first edition's early books with benefit of hindsight, increasing the histiroicity of the Orders was big on our to-do list. The gameline hasn't ever been as &quot;Atlantis! Then nothing ever changes!&quot; as it's sometimes made out to be - the Mysterium being created from the Pancryptiates and Keepers by the Corpus Author, the Arrow abandoning mortal society after World War 2, the Nameless War and the Great Refusal are all in those early books, but we leant into it hard in second edition. So yeah, I know what the Fourth Great Ministry of Seers was before Panopticon took their place, and just as we showed in Dark Eras where the Diamond gets a lot of its terminology and beliefs from, we have taken the few centuries gap between the Tremere becoming liches and being found out and driven into hiding by the Diamond and made them a former Diamond Order. Part of that was deciding what of the modern Pentacle's beliefs traces back to them, and the Dragon won.<br /> <br /> A lot of Awakening's setting, in my tenure, has been &quot;this thing first ed said they believe. What evidence do they actually have for it, how did they arrive at that hypothesis, and when did it become accepted?&quot; Often using the language or mythology the words for things come from as a guide. Retrofitting the Awakened into being <i>competent</i> academics instead of just metaphors for them.<br /> <br /> Which is pertinent to the other thread going on at the moment, about challenging Supernal &quot;truth&quot;. First ed Mage was interested in telling you mages knew the truth. We're interested in showing you how and why they know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>you guys did a pretty good job of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T15:01:20-08:00","id":1182397,"title":"","content":"As Nicolas Milioni said, good job. <br /> <br /> Too bad a good number of people will never see it. The downside of \u201cwrite the corebooks from the monsters\u2019 perspectives\u201d prevalent in CoD books is that people keep mistaking in-character beliefs and perspectives for meta-game canon and truth.<br /> <br /> It happened with Mage, with some thinking mages cannot possibly be monsters, and some thinking how mages categorizing other supernaturals is Mage invalidating their gamelines. It happened with Beast, with some people thinking the book endorsed sadism and victim-blaming. It happened with Changeling, with some people insistent on changelings being absolutely non-predatory creatures.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s both a feature and a major downside of games about playing monsters. Inevitable, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Editted out what could be an attack against preferences. 02-04-2018, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T20:07:13-08:00","id":1182482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1182397#post1182397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It happened with Beast, with some people thinking the book endorsed sadism and victim-blaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside of clinical psychology, sadism is defined as &quot;any enjoyment in being cruel,&quot; so its hard to say that beings whose existence revolves around satisfaction via terrorizing people are not encouraged to be sadistic; and the vast majority of the flavor text articles on them feeding revolves around a revenge fantasy motif.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T20:24:03-08:00","id":1182488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1182482#post1182482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of clinical psychology, sadism is defined as &quot;any enjoyment in being cruel,&quot; so its hard to say that beings whose existence revolves around satisfaction via terrorizing people are not encouraged to be sadistic;</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Fictional characters possessing this quality is not an endorsement of this quality any more than fictional vampires drinking blood and enjoying it is an endorsement of blood-drinking</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the vast majority of the flavor text articles on them feeding revolves around a revenge fantasy motif. </div> </div> </div>&quot;The vast majority&quot; is not a phrase synonymous with &quot;some.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T20:27:48-08:00","id":1182489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1182482#post1182482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of clinical psychology, sadism is defined as &quot;any enjoyment in being cruel,&quot; so its hard to say that beings whose existence revolves around satisfaction via terrorizing people are not encouraged to be sadistic; and the vast majority of the flavor text articles on them feeding revolves around a revenge fantasy motif.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is also pretty normal behavior for a wide majority of the other splats, and yet Beast gets called out for it because the game just happens to own it more than the rest. Where the complaint comes from is that people latch onto that but also brush off the ways Beasts actually try to build with their nature rather than dress it down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T20:05:23-08:00","id":1182786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1182488#post1182488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fictional characters</div> </div> </div> </div>My post was clearly referring to their in character behavior aspect alone, so... here's your reply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179633-how-does-quiescence-work-in-a-society-that-believes-in-magic?p=1182489#post1182489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is also pretty normal behavior for a wide majority of the other splats, and yet Beast gets called out for it because the game just happens to own it</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Beast is called out for it because deriving pleasure from cruelty (sadism) is to Beasts is their feeding mechanic; its at best a vice for other types and the daily bread of Beasts. Likewise, the tone of, say, Vampire is unvarying condemnation of the protagonists (and, mechanically, cruel behavior is punished by the rules), while for Beast, it is glowing praise.<br /> <br /> As far as the perceived victim blaming element, it led to them flat out making it so Heroes aren't the nearly irrevocably traumatized victims of Beasts anymore, so for whatever reason the developers seem to have taken that criticism to heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T20:26:52-08:00","id":1182788,"title":"","content":"Since I'm currently at work and can't really say much more than a brief bit, I will exhort you to make a thread in Beast about this if you are set on having this conversation. No need for us to derail this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}